n the lesson plan, and provide one<br>sentence summarizing the key difference<br>(for reporting ‘AI-driven revision’ in the<br>paper).|Returns a ready-to-paste Step 2 (6-minute script<br>+ materials + participation norms + sentence<br>frames<br>+<br>link<br>to<br>Prediction–Evidence<br>verification) and a one-sentence difference<br>statement.|Adopt. Final Step 2 replaces<br>“picture + general discussion”<br>with<br>an<br>info-gap<br>clue-card<br>prediction<br>task<br>that<br>requires<br>evidence-based<br>language<br>and<br>follow-up questioning (still within<br>≤6 minutes).|\n\n\n\n_Note. Date: June 10, 2024; Tool: Kimi; Model: moonshot-v1-20240416; Access: web interface; Interaction language: Chinese; Generation settings: default; Lesson: Lesson 3 (Listening and Talking: Plan a camp for teenagers)._ \n\n40 \n\nAppendix B. _A sample prompt sheet for using KBDeX visualizations and data in performing reflective assessment_ \n\nDate:                    Group Members: \n\n|Inquiry topic:|||\n|---|---|---|\n|**Our Analysis**<br>Analyzing our KB<br>dialogue using KB<br>visualizations and data<br>|1. What do you think about<br>your inquiry process against<br>the KBDex Growth Curve of<br>dialogues’ cumulative degree<br>centrality?<br>|Growth curve of cumulative<br>degree centrality and idea-<br>network map of<br>ideas/keywords generated by<br>f|\n||2. Which aspects have your<br>groups discussed, which<br>aspects have discussed more<br>against KBDeX idea-network<br>map of keywords?<br>e-pr|oo|\n|**Our Problems**<br>|1. Do you have made your<br>inquiries progressively be<br>deepened? And why?<br>l Pr||\n|What problems have we<br>discovered?<br>Jo|2. Which aspects do you think<br>you need to deepen but have<br>discussed less against KBDeX<br>idea-network map of<br>keywords? And why?<br>urna||\n|**Our Plan**<br>Action plans for further<br>developing our inquiry<br>|1. Which aspects are you going<br>to deepen your inquiry with the<br>help of KBDeX idea-network<br>map? And why?<b